{"title":"1972 AHSME Problems/Problem 32","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/3/70397cee672d74352b46bfc4ca356c3d1cab26a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] real t=pi/12;real u=8*t; real cu=cos(u);real su=sin(u); draw(unitcircle); draw((cos(-t),sin(-t))--(cos(13*t),sin(13*t))); draw((cu,su)--(cu,-su)); label(&quot;A&quot;,(cos(13*t),sin(13*t)),W); label(&quot;B&quot;,(cos(-t),sin(-t)),E); label(&quot;C&quot;,(cu,su),N); label(&quot;D&quot;,(cu,-su),S); label(&quot;E&quot;,(cu,sin(-t)),NE); label(&quot;2&quot;,((cu-1)/2,sin(-t)),N); label(&quot;6&quot;,((cu+1)/2,sin(-t)),N); label(&quot;3&quot;,(cu,(sin(-t)-su)/2),E); //Credit to Zimbalono for the diagram[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"228\" />\n</p><p>Chords <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> in the circle above intersect at E and are perpendicular to each other. \nIf segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5bae0aebb58216755532f548f51fb1ae2c739e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE, EB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc2afec04e3636c80fa3d89e5468045595151c4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ED$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> have measures <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1ac8effbba9c83e52fc90ea5a0c3269f872dbbbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> respectively, then the length of the diameter of the circle is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f2900714f28da1f3aede82b9e3334a993794a723.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }4\\sqrt{5}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\sqrt{65}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }2\\sqrt{17}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }3\\sqrt{7}\\qquad  \\textbf{(E) }6\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"484\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the chord theorem we can immediately solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/8/9e8502d2aceb4bd11a0f30823d6887873d1ca604.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {CE}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> which will help us. The chord theorem states that if two chords, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238f77f5bd36cadced68f029e4554015289e50ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {AB}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/3/7c337e833a82ec0650a1a82a4443a76307ebe7c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {CD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />, intersect at lets say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db4d45ebbf9c7e568325fd3a3792d1ec4cfcd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {AE} \\cdot \\overline {EB}=\\overline {CE} \\cdot \\overline {ED}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" />. Now that we know this we can label length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/8/9e8502d2aceb4bd11a0f30823d6887873d1ca604.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {CE}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/a/03a45952f8115322d2879f7d090126f059757ba0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\eta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"9\" height=\"11\" />. We now have the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cbc625dd11435a60daa0348d54d10d587bc3847.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\eta=2\\cdot6\\implies3\\eta=12\\implies\\eta=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"279\" height=\"17\" />. We now know the chord lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We now label the center of the circle as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. If the circle was on the graph, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> being right on the origin, then make a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> line cutting through the center. This bisects chord <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae2cf3b47570f346ef95b838bf586ecc7dfcf9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {AM}=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e94091ace7af155ef4221c1601bcc357ecd5b93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {EM}=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> If we now draw a \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89f09c84538ec43930ca5d8e5e0957e2000822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />\" line which bisects chord <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/1/d71d65526b571a26e1c8ccc1c07e5431dd24e5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {CN}=\\tfrac{7}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"68\" height=\"24\" />. If we now move up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/0070705652cb9ee577aba96a28fafd3a0c69050c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {EM}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/4/da4ebabbfb25086d7c67b022f1168e4924d39b72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {ON}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> then we can find the radius(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/e/e3ef16a00c61d61fa575a05b542aff0c4f9ce994.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {CO}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />) using Pythagorean Theorem.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/a/9fa6c2b693f4ee95cb7dc5bae5b3cb4b11dc5519.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{{\\overline {EM}}^2+{\\overline {ON}}^2}=r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"155\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/d/41dac665e10f032665176eb3a46534d2c50b4d75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2^2+(\\tfrac{7}{2})^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"91\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/b/c6b687085688657fd527e116d71f6a046d493c58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{4+\\frac{49}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"73\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/e/69e753b90e9d73356488903858f158cbddb66016.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{65}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"42\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/5/4b5a9b857e06d40e0c070ae1f0e01c8320656abf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{65}}{2}=r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"72\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Now that we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, the diameter is just two times of that, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6dd75d891d8e2524e74538fc4e07bc900b574ec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\sqrt{65}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Am24\">~AM24</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017171001\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.024 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 138/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7522/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:18015:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017171001 and revision id 258712. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}